An electronic signature qualifies as an advanced electronic signature when it satisfies all of the following requirements (E Art. 26):
- it is uniquely linked to the signatory (E Art. 26(a));  
- it is capable of identifying the signatory (E Art. 26(b));  
- it is created using electronic signature creation data that the signatory can, with a high level of confidence, use under his sole control (E Art. 26(c)); and  
- it is linked to the data signed therewith in such a way that any subsequent change in the data is detectable (E Art. 26(d)).

Compliance with those requirements is presumed where an advanced electronic signature meets reference standards established by Commission implementing acts (E Art. 27(4)).
